::ALG2_U03_L08_GP01::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U03_L08_GP01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>Unit 3 standards synthesis; no new primary MLA standard<br><br>Question:<br>Simplify &radic;72. {
= 6&radic;2#Correct. 72 = 36*2 and the square root of 36 is 6.
~ 36&radic;2#The square root of 36 is 6, not 36.
~ 8&radic;9#The perfect square factor should be rooted.
~ 12&radic;6#This does not square back to 72.
}

::ALG2_U03_L08_GP02::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U03_L08_GP02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>Unit 3 standards synthesis; no new primary MLA standard<br><br>Question:<br>What is the domain of f(x)=&radic;(x-6)? {
~ x &le; 6#That allows negative radicands.
= x &ge; 6#Correct. The radicand must be nonnegative: x - 6 >= 0.
~ x &ne; 6#x = 6 is allowed.
~ all real numbers#Inputs less than 6 are not allowed.
}

::ALG2_U03_L08_GP03::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U03_L08_GP03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>Unit 3 standards synthesis; no new primary MLA standard<br><br>Question:<br>Solve &radic;(x+3)=5. {
~ x = 2#This subtracts from 5 instead of 25.
~ x = 28#This adds 3 instead of subtracting it.
= x = 22#Correct. Square both sides to get x + 3 = 25.
~ x = 5#This is the square root value, not x.
}

::ALG2_U03_L08_GP04::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U03_L08_GP04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>Unit 3 standards synthesis; no new primary MLA standard<br><br>Question:<br>Simplify (x<sup>2</sup>-16)/(x-4). {
~ x - 4, x &ne; 4#The remaining factor is x + 4.
~ x + 4, no restriction#The original denominator excludes 4.
~ x<sup>2</sup>+4#The numerator must be factored.
= x + 4, x &ne; 4#Correct. Factor and cancel x - 4 while keeping the original restriction.
}

::ALG2_U03_L08_GP05::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U03_L08_GP05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>Unit 3 standards synthesis; no new primary MLA standard<br><br>Question:<br>What is the vertical asymptote of f(x)=7/(x+2)? {
= x = -2#Correct. Set x + 2 equal to 0.
~ x = 2#The sign is reversed.
~ y = -2#Vertical asymptotes use x = value.
~ y = 7#The numerator is not the asymptote.
}

